# Search

This run uses Research First Search. Research and its reviewed findings accumulate on the Board. A Planner writes a research proposal as a compiled PDF. A Committee judges the waiting proposals and assigns the free project slots. One Worker session conducts each accepted project end to end — code, experiments, analysis, and the final report PDF. When the proposal says the project is scored, the framework scores the project's output directory after the Worker session ends; a study is never scored. A Reviewer then compares the proposal, the report, the artifacts, and, for a scored project, the framework score. Every proposal, decision, worker artifact, report, score, and review is published into the Research First Board — a filesystem folder per plan — and later Planner and Committee calls read the Board directly. Treat a Worker's source, attempt, and report as published only when that plan's `worker/manifest.json` exists. The Search does not infer a stop from failed work, rejected proposals, empty Committee rounds, or stalled scores. The Committee can deliberately end it through the funded-nothing path when the remaining time cannot fit another candidate's execution and scoring or every direction is exhausted. Budget and any explicitly configured project cap also limit execution.
